{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789224841,"nonce":"PqBLmniING/AjGpzM3H39y6xDBY=","title":"--mode jit is slower than the interpreter on binary_trees","message":"Compiling everything up front (--mode jit) runs bench/binary_trees.wren in 2.8 s of CPU versus 2.1 s interpreted and 0.7 s tiered (2026-09-12, Immix default). The eager compile has no inline-cache snapshot or type profile, so every call stays a generic dispatch and every arithmetic op stays boxed, and it also loses the interpreter's own IC fast paths. Either seed the eager compile with CHA-planted caches and blind Num speculation the way the tiered path does after warm-up, or document the mode as a correctness lane rather than a performance one.","files":null}]}